# Scratch at the repository root (17.5)
#
# Every `>` redirect in this working copy lands here, and five had accumulated
# by 22 September: a UTF-16 dump of lambda/composition/cleanup.py taken before
# SUBJ-01 changed it, three query results from that investigation, and an empty
# log. None had ever been committed, and none held anything the repository did
# not already have in a newer form.
#
# ANCHORED TO THE ROOT with a leading slash, deliberately. A bare *.txt would
# also catch lambda/layers/docprocessing/requirements.txt, which is tracked and
# is what the docprocessing layer is built from - ignoring it would not
# untrack it, but it would hide a real edit to it from `git status`, which is
# the one place that edit has to be visible.
#
# A .txt at the root that IS worth keeping can be forced in with `git add -f`,
# or given its own negation below.
/*.txt
